# Review: CloudflarePlugin

The connector is built as specified: one lazily loaded module contributes a `ConnectorEntry` on
`ConnectorEvents.Start` with the `cloudflare.com` source, `OAuthProvider.CLOUDFLARE` and the scope list
from `GET /oauth/scopes`; `onTokenCreated` labels the token from `/user` with an `/accounts` fallback and
`testConnection` maps failures to `ConnectionTestError`. What is weak is testing: `cloudflare-api.test.ts`
covers only the HTTP helpers (`fetchUser`, `fetchAccounts`, a 403 failing as an HTTP error), never the
connector hooks themselves, so none of the three acceptance tests runs end to end.

Of 4 items: 0 done, 1 untested, 2 partial, 0 diverged, 1 missing.

