```mdl
verdict CloudflareConnector: The connector entry, OAuth scopes, label hook and connection test are implemented; no test drives the hooks.
  status: untested
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-cloudflare/dx.config.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-cloudflare/src/capabilities/connector.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-cloudflare/src/constants.ts#CLOUDFLARE_OAUTH_SCOPES, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-cloudflare/src/services/cloudflare-api.ts#fetchUser, github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-cloudflare/src/services/cloudflare-api.ts#fetchAccounts]
  walkthrough:
    - The lazy module activates on ConnectorEvents.Start and provides the Connector capability. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-cloudflare/dx.config.ts
    - The module contributes the entry with OAuth provider, scopes, onTokenCreated (email, username, then first account name, under orDie) and testConnection (GET /accounts mapped to ConnectionTestError). github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-cloudflare/src/capabilities/connector.ts
    - The scope ids are the GET /oauth/scopes names, without offline_access. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-cloudflare/src/constants.ts#CLOUDFLARE_OAUTH_SCOPES
    - The v4 helpers send the bearer token, unwrap the envelope and retry 429/5xx. github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-cloudflare/src/services/cloudflare-api.ts#fetchUser
  note: |
    Matches the spec, including the early return when `accessToken.account` is already set. The only test
    (`cloudflare-api.test.ts`) exercises the HTTP helpers, not `onTokenCreated` or `testConnection`.
```

